scores = [4,8,3,1,0]

number1, number2, number3, number4, number5 = scores
print(number1, number2, number3, number4, number5, sep="\n")

unpack doesnt change the original values from the scores variable, however if you want to unpack only two it will throw an error of ValueError of too many values to unpack if you don't specify where to put the remaining values in the list.

how to resolve that, we would need to specify where the rest will be:

number1, number2, *others = scores  //use (wildcard *) to collect the remaining items into a list

when unpacking small many elemnts into too many variables: not enough values to unpack. The number of variables must match the number of items 

